{"kind":"assert","text":"Draft 3 of the client design note answers review 98d6a650.\nBranch `planner/client-primitive-note-20261113`, commit 2ef973ed,\nfile `notes/2026-11-13-scope-client.md`. Hugh ratifies it.\n\nGap A. Section 3 defines the present values of a request: the\ndraft's values while the member has the draft, and the values of\nthe latest signing while the request is pending. Rules 1 and 2\nof section 6 compare the sealed meaning with the present values.\nValues that differ continue as a new draft with a new key. `edit`\nchanges only a draft in the state `editing`. Invariant 4 covers\neach value that the member typed and did not discard.\n\nGap B. `Custody` gains `absent(identity, signing, head)`. Section\n7 has the row: for a dead signing with a copy that has no answer,\nthe client reads the journal one time and calls `absent`.\n\nCorrections:\n1. The fourth case of section 2 says \"can still be posted\" only\n   after Ben removes a comment.\n2. A key shows in a slot or in the list, never in both. Rows are\n   apart. A waiting `other-recorded` request keeps the old key\n   and that status, and the new key starts at the `restore`.\n3. Invariant 1 counts intentions and continuations.\n4. Section 5.2 includes the phase `prepared`.\n5. C1 needs RC-1.\n6. The stop `taken` covers `locked` and `conflicting`. Each\n   store port signals a change by another client.\n7. A discarded or dismissed request can still take effect, and\n   its row shows with no notice.\n\nThe custody model, the status rules and the order of work do not\nchange.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}